# SAFIA.OS — contact transmission (EmailJS)
#
# Copy this file to `.env` and fill in the three values from
# https://dashboard.emailjs.com. Until they are set, the contact form falls back
# to opening the visitor's mail client with the message pre-filled — it never
# pretends to have sent something.
#
# IMPORTANT: everything prefixed with VITE_ is inlined into the public client
# bundle. Only EmailJS's PUBLIC key belongs here. Never put a private key,
# password, or API secret in a VITE_ variable. Restrict the public key to your
# deployed domain in the EmailJS dashboard.
#
# `.env` is git-ignored; `.env.example` is the committed template.

VITE_EMAILJS_SERVICE_ID=
VITE_EMAILJS_TEMPLATE_ID=
VITE_EMAILJS_PUBLIC_KEY=

# The EmailJS template should reference these variables:
#   {{from_name}}  {{reply_to}}  {{message}}  {{to_email}}
